From 3a3909cec88773851085ed9073c7ceec30427064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:21:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers of Trilinos: conversion on the GPU, fourth review

The matrices of hypre are converted to Tpetra by kernels of Kokkos, where
Tpetra computes, from the arrays of hypre on the GPU when hypre computes
there (the rows are permuted, merged and sorted by insertion in parallel).
On the beam of 421,443 unknowns on the GPU, the conversion takes 0.064
seconds instead of 0.49 (0.029 instead of 0.45 on the Laplace equation of
2,146,689 unknowns).

Fourth review:
- the node of the host is the serial node, used only when the default
  node computes on a GPU: with Kokkos built for a GPU, some products of
  sparse matrices of Tpetra run in the default execution space on the
  data of the OpenMP node;
- the solvers of Belos are built again when the matrix changes (PCPG kept
  a seed space only valid for the same matrix), except GCRODR, which keeps
  its recycled subspace for the matrices of the same rows;
- placement: FROSch on the GPU when Trilinos is built for one, the GPU
  for all the entries when Tpetra has no node of the host; Tacho uses the
  default node (it computes in the default execution space of Kokkos);
- MueLu: the rigid body modes and the coordinates are given in all the
  syntaxes; a failed reuse of the hierarchy builds it again;
- CMake: the configuration files of Kokkos are also compared by their
  contents (copies in views of Spack);
- tests: the reuse of the whole hierarchy changes the iterations (the
  hierarchy is indeed reused), LSQR and the native GMRES of Tpetra accept
  parameters absent from their lists;
- docs: kept smoothers and Chebyshev eigenvalue under reuse, rigid body
  modes per syntax, FROSch and Tacho on the GPU, restarts of GMRES.
